hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"16720","He said: Abu al-Nadr narrated to us, he said: Shayban narrated to us, from Ashath, he said: an old man from Banu Malik ibn Kinana narrated to me, he said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at the market of Dhu al-Majaz threading through it saying: O people, say: There is no god but Allah, you will prosper; he said: And Abu Jahl was throwing dust on him and saying: O people, let not this one delude you from your religion, for he only wants you to leave your gods and leave al-Lat and al-Uzza; he said: And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not turn toward him; he said: We said: Describe the Messenger for us; he said: Between two red cloaks, of medium stature, full-fleshed, handsome of face, intensely black of hair, intensely white, with flowing hair."
